<title>POLAND: Polish zloty fix stronger at 3.21 pct from parity.</title>
<headline>Polish zloty fix stronger at 3.21 pct from parity.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.0110 against the dollar, down from 3.0025 on Monday and at 1.8000 to the mark, up from 1.8150, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 3.21 percent from the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, stronger than Monday's fixing at 2.99 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
